  "ci/affected-graph/cargo_moon_parity.py:3517": "Fixed in ba9b1ed9. The exclusion is now `(?!as\\s+\\$[A-Za-z_])`, so it skips only a jq variable binding such as `else . as $rows`. New rows: `source as arg` with an `as` file that holds `uv sync` reds, and the same script without the `as` file raises `MoonOutputError`. The real tree still passes. A mutation test (the broad `(?!as\\s)` put back) makes the self-test fail."
}

{
  "ci/affected-graph/cargo_moon_parity.py:3505": "Fixed in fd982eec. `UV_SOURCE_STMT_RE` now accepts `{` and `!` as prefixes. New self-test row: a project script with `{ source ./mutate.sh; }`, where `mutate.sh` holds `uv sync`, reds. A mutation test (`{` removed in memory) makes the self-test fail. The matcher also skips `. as` and `source as`, because the jq idiom `else . as $rows` (`ci/moon-diagnosis/run.sh:278`) is not a shell source statement."
}

{
  "ci/affected-graph/cargo_moon_parity.py:3336": "Fixed in 63d151fe. The new `_uv_words` tokenizes each uv invocation with shell quote and escape rules. Only an unquoted, unescaped word that starts with `#` starts a comment. `shlex` was not used, because a probe showed it splits `a#b` as `['a']`. New red rows: `a\\ #settings.env` and `\"a #settings.env\"` with `--reinstall`. `a#b` stays one word. On an unmatched quote, `--isolated` gets no credit, and a mutating flag anywhere still reds. Mutation tests (a naive split, shlex with `#` as commenter, and `--isolated` credit on an unmatched quote) each make the self-test fail.",
  "ci/affected-graph/cargo_moon_parity.py:3446": "Fixed in 63d151fe. A14's closure now uses its own matcher, `UV_SOURCE_STMT_RE`. It accepts `source` or `.` after `;`, `&`, `|`, `(`, `then`, `do` or `else`. The shared `SOURCE_STMT_RE` is unchanged, so what A8 and A10 follow does not change (SMA-605). The cycle guard and the fail-closed `MoonOutputError` on an unresolved path are kept. New rows: `true; source ./mutate.sh`, `x && . ./mutate.sh`, `if ...; then source ...; fi`, and an unresolved mid-line path. A mutation test (the line-start regex put back) makes the self-test fail."
}

